The one-line horror
if ( file_exists( $path ) ) {
    // ... use the cached file
}
Nothing about that line looks dangerous. It's the kind of guard clause you've written a thousand times. But suppose $path is:
s3://my-bucket/cache/style-4f2a.css
Now that single file_exists() is not a syscall. It's a HeadObject request to Amazon S3 — a network round trip that leaves your server, waits for S3, and co...

